---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { failureStates } from "../content/institute-site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Ethotechnics Institute"
  description="Open standards for high-stakes systems that must remain reversible under failure."
>
  <section class="institute-hero stack-lg">
    <h1>Open standards for high-stakes systems that must remain reversible under failure.</h1>
    <p>Stoppability rules, reversal clocks, burden ceilings, contestability mechanics.</p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button primary" href="/#failure-intake">Start with a failure</a>
      <a class="muted" href="/how-it-works">New here? See how this works →</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="failure-intake" class="stack-lg">
    <h2>What’s not holding?</h2>
    <p>Choose the closest match. This is about routing, not blame.</p>
    <div class="failure-grid" aria-label="Failure routing options">
      {failureStates.map((state) => (
        <a class="button" href={`/failure/${state.slug}`}>
          {state.shortLabel}
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="small muted">Each path routes to a ready-to-use governance artifact.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-lg">
    <h2>How to adopt Ethotechnics</h2>
    <p>
      Choose the route that matches how your organization actually takes responsibility: policy,
      operations, or build.
    </p>
    <div class="adopt-grid">
      <article class="card stack-sm">
        <h3>Legal / Compliance / Risk</h3>
        <h4>Artifacts</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Decision record template</li>
          <li>Reversal SLA template</li>
          <li>Contestability &amp; appeals playbook</li>
        </ul>
        <h4>Metrics</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Reversal latency</li>
          <li>Time-in-harm</li>
        </ul>
        <h4>First-week checklist</h4>
        <ol>
          <li>Name decision owners</li>
          <li>Define reversal authority</li>
          <li>Set appeal time bounds</li>
          <li>Publish burden ceilings</li>
          <li>Identify freeze conditions</li>
        </ol>
      </article>

      <article class="card stack-sm">
        <h3>Appeals / Incident response</h3>
        <h4>Artifacts</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Escalation ladder / freeze authority table</li>
          <li>Harm receipt format</li>
          <li>Reversal SLA template</li>
        </ul>
        <h4>Metrics</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Appeal clearance time</li>
          <li>Burden hours per case</li>
        </ul>
        <h4>First-week checklist</h4>
        <ol>
          <li>Map queues</li>
          <li>Assign freeze roles</li>
          <li>Define escalation clocks</li>
          <li>Set claimant time caps</li>
          <li>Run one tabletop</li>
        </ol>
      </article>

      <article class="card stack-sm">
        <h3>Product / Engineering</h3>
        <h4>Artifacts</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Decision record system</li>
          <li>Freeze authority table</li>
          <li>Reversal testing checklist</li>
        </ul>
        <h4>Metrics</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Mean time to stop</li>
          <li>Reversal success rate</li>
        </ul>
        <h4>First-week checklist</h4>
        <ol>
          <li>Instrument reversibility</li>
          <li>Bind ownership to code paths</li>
          <li>Test rollback</li>
          <li>Log reversals</li>
          <li>Fail one drill intentionally</li>
        </ol>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="small"><strong>If you cannot complete the first-week checklist, pause adoption until the system is ready.</strong></p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
